{"units": [{"id": "asson-def1", "translation": "nearer"}, {"id": "asson-note1", "translation": "Superlative ἄσσιστα [nearest] means 'proxime' [very near]. Hesychius fr. 62 explains it by έγγιστα [nearest]."}, {"id": "asson-quote1", "translation": "But Sisyphus came near to Anticlea."}, {"id": "asson-word1", "translation": "nearest"}, {"id": "asson-word2", "translation": "nearest"}, {"id": "asso-orth1", "translation": "to rush"}, {"id": "asso-def1", "translation": "I rush"}, {"id": "asso-note1", "translation": "[ϊξ' is a corruption in some copies for τησ.]"}, {"id": "asso-quote1", "translation": "horned one: with maddened leap he rushed toward — fear of Cerchneia."}, {"id": "asso-quote2", "translation": "you rushed along the — path."}, {"id": "asso-word1", "translation": "rushed"}, {"id": "asso-word2", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "astakos-orth1", "translation": "Astacus"}, {"id": "astakos-def1", "translation": "Astacus, father of Melanippus, the Theban leader"}, {"id": "astaspes-orth1", "translation": "Astaspes"}, {"id": "astaspes-def1", "translation": "Persian proper name"}, {"id": "astektos-orth1", "translation": "unbearable"}, {"id": "astektos-def1", "translation": "that cannot be contained"}, {"id": "astektos-quote1", "translation": "ἄστερκτα: things that cannot be held back. Aeschylus in Semele (fr. 220)."}, {"id": "astektos-quote2", "translation": "ἄστεκτα: unbearable, things that cannot be held back."}, {"id": "astenakti-orth1", "translation": "without groaning"}, {"id": "astenakti-def1", "translation": "without groaning"}, {"id": "astenakti-quote1", "translation": "who endured without a groan like a tuna."}, {"id": "asterganor-orth1", "translation": "not loving men"}, {"id": "asterganor-def1", "translation": "not loving men"}, {"id": "asterganor-quote1", "translation": "virginity that does not love men."}, {"id": "asteropos-orth1", "translation": "star-faced, shining"}, {"id": "asteropos-def1", "translation": "having a starry face, shining"}, {"id": "asteropos-note1", "translation": "of the moon"}, {"id": "asteropos-quote1", "translation": "the starry eye of Leto's daughter."}, {"id": "aster-orth1", "translation": "star"}, {"id": "aster-def1", "translation": "star"}, {"id": "aster-note1", "translation": "[ἀστέρας [stars] in a spurious verse Ag. 7.]"}, {"id": "aster-word1", "translation": "stars"}, {"id": "astibes-orth1", "translation": "untrodden"}, {"id": "astibes-def1", "translation": "not trodden"}, {"id": "astibes-quote1", "translation": "the untrodden land for Apollo."}, {"id": "astikos-orth1", "translation": "of the city, civic"}, {"id": "astikos-def1", "translation": "urban"}, {"id": "astikos-note1", "translation": "where Hermann reads ἀστικός [of the city] as at v. 997."}, {"id": "astikos-quote1", "translation": "the city people."}, {"id": "astikos-quote2", "translation": "the city altars,"}, {"id": "astikos-quote3", "translation": "speaking of a double pollution, both foreign and of the city."}, {"id": "astikos-quote4", "translation": "the Attic people,"}, {"id": "astikos-word1", "translation": "of the city"}, {"id": "astonos-orth1", "translation": "without groaning"}, {"id": "astonos-note1", "translation": "[Sept. 859 corruptly for ναύστολος [ship-sent], which see.]"}, {"id": "astonos-word1", "translation": "ship-sent"}, {"id": "astoxenos-orth1", "translation": "stranger, guest"}, {"id": "astoxenos-def1", "translation": "guest"}, {"id": "astoxenos-note1", "translation": "See Thes. vol 1, 2 p.2252."}, {"id": "astoxenos-quote1", "translation": "May this matter be without harm from strangers."}, {"id": "astos-orth1", "translation": "citizen"}, {"id": "astos-def1", "translation": "citizen"}, {"id": "astos-quote1", "translation": "they are hymned by the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote2", "translation": "seeing this age of the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote3", "translation": "leaving to the citizens irresistible tumults."}, {"id": "astos-quote4", "translation": "heavy is the voice of the citizens with wrath."}, {"id": "astos-quote5", "translation": "to proclaim to the citizens a cry to this house."}, {"id": "astos-quote6", "translation": "mighty hatred among the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote7", "translation": "hatred of the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote8", "translation": "some other of the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote9", "translation": "the best of my citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote10", "translation": "reverence of the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote11", "translation": "I advise to honor that which is neither anarchic nor despotic, protecting it for the citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote12", "translation": "I extended this advice to my citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote13", "translation": "honored by these citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote14", "translation": "among my citizens."}, {"id": "astos-quote15", "translation": "for the citizens to prosper and not to weary with time."}, {"id": "astos-quote16", "translation": "to the citizens of Pallas."}, {"id": "astos-quote17", "translation": "having shared with all the citizens about these things."}, {"id": "astos-quote18", "translation": "may a swarm of diseases, unpleasant, sit upon the citizens' heads."}, {"id": "astos-quote19", "translation": "I am the protector, and all the citizens."}, {"id": "astrabizo-orth1", "translation": "to be like a beast of burden"}, {"id": "astrabizo-def1", "translation": "I am like a beast of burden"}, {"id": "astrabizo-quote1", "translation": "I hear that the Indian nomads ride on camels like beasts of burden."}, {"id": "astrape-orth1", "translation": "lightning"}, {"id": "astrape-def1", "translation": "lightning"}, {"id": "astrape-quote1", "translation": "the lightnings and thunderbolts."}, {"id": "astrape-quote2", "translation": "with bright flashes the gleam of torches."}, {"id": "astrapto-orth1", "translation": "to flash lightning"}, {"id": "astrapto-def1", "translation": "I flash lightning"}, {"id": "astrapto-quote1", "translation": "from her eyes flashed a Gorgon-like gleam."}, {"id": "astrogeiton-orth1", "translation": "neighboring the stars"}, {"id": "astrogeiton-def1", "translation": "neighboring the stars"}, {"id": "astrogeiton-quote1", "translation": "star-neighboring peaks."}, {"id": "astron-orth1", "translation": "star"}, {"id": "astron-def1", "translation": "star"}, {"id": "astron-quote1", "translation": "I showed the risings of the stars."}, {"id": "astron-quote2", "translation": "the paths of the heavenly stars."}, {"id": "astron-quote3", "translation": "I know the assembly of the night stars."}, {"id": "astron-quote4", "translation": "so that neither before the time nor beyond the stars a vain missile might fall."}, {"id": "astron-quote5", "translation": "the sky blazing beneath the stars."}, {"id": "astron-quote6", "translation": "bright is the full moon in the middle of the shield, the eldest of the stars."}, {"id": "astron-quote7", "translation": "night gleaming with stars."}, {"id": "astrophos-orth1", "translation": "not turning back"}, {"id": "astrophos-def1", "translation": "not turned back"}, {"id": "astrophos-quote1", "translation": "with eyes that do not turn."}, {"id": "asty-orth1", "translation": "city"}, {"id": "asty-def1", "translation": "city"}, {"id": "asty-quote1", "translation": "the city of the Cadmeans."}, {"id": "asty-quote2", "translation": "the city of the Persians."}, {"id": "asty-quote3", "translation": "the great empty city of Susa,"}, {"id": "asty-quote4", "translation": "the city of Susa and Ecbatana."}, {"id": "asty-quote5", "translation": "the city of Susa."}, {"id": "asty-quote6", "translation": "this city of Susa."}, {"id": "asty-quote7", "translation": "a cry throughout the city."}, {"id": "asty-quote8", "translation": "safety is theirs as they walk through the city (ἄστεος [of the city] written above in M)."}, {"id": "asty-quote9", "translation": "the city of Teuthras of the Mysians."}, {"id": "asty-quote10", "translation": "through the city"}, {"id": "astyanax-orth1", "translation": "Astyanax"}]}